<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria sells 10 bln levs 3-mth coupon T-bills.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria sells 10 bln levs 3-mth coupon T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's Finance Ministry on Wednesday sold 10 billion levs of three-month floater coupon T-bills, yielding 61.27 percent to maturity, the central bank said.</p>
<p>The issue was offered with no par value or minimum acceptable price set in advance by the ministry.</p>
<p>The coupon equals the central bank main interest rate, now set at 18 percent monthly or 216 percent annually.</p>
<p>Details of the issue follow. Prices are in percent of par:</p>
<p> Issue number		  BG3021297026</p>
<p> Type			    floater coupon</p>
<p> Term			    three months</p>
<p> Auction date		  March 12</p>
<p> Issue date		    March 12</p>
<p> Maturity date		 June 11</p>
<p> Bids received		 10,040 million levs</p>
<p> Avg price of bids	   95.37</p>
<p> Bids approved		 10,000 million levs</p>
<p> Avg accepted price	  95.40 pct</p>
<p> Avg yield to maturity     61.27 pct @</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 981 8569</p>
